# Which 1Password item holds the write token for each GitHub owner.
# extras/gh-readonly-tokens.sh writes this file for you. This copy is the format
# reference, for reading a map by hand or fixing one entry without a full re-run.
#
# By hand: copy to ~/.config/gh-shim/write-tokens, chmod 600, fill in your refs.
#
#   <github-owner>  <1password-account>  op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
#
# Right-click the token field in 1Password and "Copy Secret Reference" to get
# the op:// value. `op account list` gives the account column.
#
# dot-local/bin/gh reads this for the write tier only. Reads and the PR
# lifecycle come from the login keychain instead, so they never touch 1Password.
# An owner with no line here falls back to `op plugin run -- gh`, which picks an
# account on its own and may well pick the wrong one.

tvrmsmith  my.1password.com  op://Private/GitHub Personal Access Token/token
